# Random modules whose predicates have bodies that are disjunctions, and
# clauses whose heads are patterns, testing their inputs against functors
# through aliases, after other goals, in `some` scopes and in nested
# disjunctions, in if-then-elses, negations and lambda expressions
# (generate-switch-programs.py). merkc must find the switches and
# disjunctions that mmc does, after common subexpression elimination.
#
# REQUIRES: mmc
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir %t
# RUN: %python %S/../../../utils/type-oracle/generate-switch-programs.py --seed 5 --count 40 %t
# RUN: %compare-switches %t/*.m
